{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Which.</b> The word בקשה is from the heavy binyan and the ḥirik indicates it, and the qof lacks the dagesh, like שלחו באש מקדשיך (Psalms 74:7), and like התל בי (1 Kings 18:27), which is from ויהתל בהם אליהו — and it has no parallel like it among all the complete verbs in masculine singular. The meaning of 'the complete': except for the guttural letters. And the reckoning in all these refers to the alef mentioned. For thus was the number of Solomon's women: seven hundred princesses and three hundred like concubines."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ויחסר הדגש מן הקו\"ף' — the qof lacks the dagesh — is standard: a guttural or quiescent alef preceding a beged-kefet letter causes the dagesh lene to drop. 'האלף הנזכר' refers back to the alef in אשר. The final comparison 'כמו פילגשים' likely means the 300 were secondary, 'like concubines' rather than full wives; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:20.167793080Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}